---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { tools, usedInputs } from '../lib/tools';
---

<Base title="About | osint-hub" description="What osint-hub is, how tools are chosen, and how to use them responsibly.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About osint-hub</h1>
    <p>
      osint-hub lists {tools.length} open-source intelligence tools, organised by the input they take. Most directories
      group tools by category. Investigations start from what you already have, such as a username, an email or a photo,
      so this one does too.
    </p>

    <h2>What each label means</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Passive / Active</dt>
      <dd>
        A passive tool only queries third-party sources and never contacts the target or its infrastructure. An active
        tool can scan, crawl or visit the target, which the target may be able to see.
      </dd>
      <dt>Account</dt>
      <dd>You need to sign up, even for the free tier.</dd>
      <dt>Where to go next</dt>
      <dd>What a tool gives you (an email, a domain, an IP) links to the tools that take it as input.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static. Filters and searches run in your browser. The "Search directly" boxes send your query straight
      from your browser to the tool, never through osint-hub, and outbound links carry no referrer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="responsible-use">Responsible use</h2>
    <p>
      These tools are listed for research, journalism, security work and personal safety. Using them to stalk, harass,
      dox or intimidate someone is harmful and often illegal. Check the laws where you are and the terms of each tool.
    </p>
    <p>
      People-search engines and face-recognition search are listed, because journalists, fraud investigators and people
      checking who is contacting them rely on them. Their pages carry a responsible-use notice, and each one is reviewed
      individually before it is added.
    </p>
    <p>
      osint-hub does not list stalkerware, doxxing services, or sites that sell leaked or breached personal data or
      credentials, including lookup bots built on leaked databases.
    </p>

    <h2>Browse by input</h2>
    <ul class="pill-links">
      {usedInputs().map((i) => <li><a href={`/inputs/${i.key}`}>{i.label} ({i.count})</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
